-- §2  Every contract's roster against the population it declares.
# One row per disagreement between a roster and its population. Empty is the correct output,
# across every contract folds/contract_subjects.sqlc counts, the laws themselves among them.
#
# The laws checking their own contract is not circular
#   It is the second witness the whole repository is built on: reports/integrity.sqlc reads the
#   roster difference off each contract's outer join, and algebra/integrity.sqlc works out the same
#   sets with EXCEPT and EXISTS. Two routes to one answer.
-- reports/integrity.sqlc, read by the example.
SELECT z.contract AS "contract!", z.problem AS "problem!", z.subject AS "subject!"
FROM (
    :compose(reports/integrity.sqlc)
) z
ORDER BY z.contract, z.subject
